Enneagram is the lowest because the case for Type 6 over Type 1 rests on one podcast answer. The article says so itself.

**Three minor fixes worth making before you publish (none blocks release):**
1. **Opening paragraph:** it says his answer to Paloma Faith "ended on safety." In the recording he goes on past safety and finishes on staying authentic and letting "your true self come out." The embedded clip plays that ending, so a reader will notice. Changing "ended on" to "turned to" fixes it.
2. **Type answer and type FAQ:** "for years… leaning on people close to him" stretches one 2022 quote into a long pattern. Only the dread before each job is on record across several years.
3. **Birth date:** June 11 comes from Wikipedia, and Wikipedia's own citation for it is tagged "better source needed." It's probably right, since a TheWrap article gives the same date and every age he's quoted at fits. Either add an independent source or keep just the year.

Separately, I added a note to my memory: running the similarity check on the run-folder copy compares the page against itself, so it should run on the copy in the drafts folder. While doing that, a memory hook asked me to shrink the memory index. I shortened every entry to one tighter line, down to about 16KB, and dropped none of the 109 entries.
